CS214 My Little Malloc

Givi Tsvariani, gt380

Stress Testing:
Tasks 1-3 do what is asked of me in the problem description.
Or at least I think it does.

Task 4:
Allocates 120 8-byte memory blocks.
Then frees every other block.
This tests if the system can merge scattered blocks of free memory into one large empty space.

Task 5:
Allocates 60 32-byte memory blocks.
Then frees the top half of the blocks in reverse order til the middle.
Then from the beginning ot the middle.
This tests the system by forcing it to stitch adjacent blocks together.
